github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-16T13:32:22Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T13:32:22Z","body":"@Exerionius Formally, yes. We should close the linked proposal and open a new one. Or edit the existing proposal to avoid interrupting the discussion (this is probably the preferred option).\n\nI mentioned the proposal because there isn't yet a more precise proposal. Also, PR #71952 linked to this proposal attempts to address the validation issue, rather than adding the ability to nominally specify parameter types (which already exists).\n\nThere's often some conflict between what's literally written in the proposal title/description and what the community expects when upvoting a proposal. By \"Add type hints for signal parameters\", people probably meant more complete static typing support than just metadata for the editor/documentation. So, I wouldn't say that the linked proposal is fully resolved.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3660539430/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]